    "resume_retry_duplication": "The launcher skips any cell that already has result+receipt; a retry would duplicate a whole cell (+2048), not +1 or +2.",
    "other": "No cell shows a deficit; excess is bounded at +2 and absent in 35/48 cells."
  },
  "preregistration_note": "Amendment 1 (A1.3) chose 2048 specifically because 2048 = 16 x 128 and stated that fixing it would make the +1 tail asymmetry 'structurally disappear'. That expectation was NOT met: the implementation stops on total >= target rather than capping at the target, so the tail can still overshoot. This is a genuine protocol deviation between the preregistration's stated rationale and the executed code.",
